Description: CVE-2026-112320 - Fix RPC leak when client switches from RPCSEC_GSS
 svc_do_xprt() retains xp_auth across calls for RPCSEC_GSS.  If the client
 switches to a different auth flavor on the same connection, the pre-existing
 xp_auth must be destroyed or the new auth handler overwrites it and leaks
 its contents, allowing remote denial of service (memory exhaustion in kadmind).
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/krb5/krb5/commit/c4288c4a2fd477f60b9390ca5a7db442055e679b
Author: Julien Rische <jrische@redhat.com>
Last-Update: 2026-11-13
---
--- a/src/lib/rpc/svc_auth.c
+++ b/src/lib/rpc/svc_auth.c
@@ -39,6 +39,8 @@
 
 #include <gssrpc/rpc.h>
 
+extern struct svc_auth_ops svc_auth_gss_ops;
+
 /*
  * Server side authenticators are called from authenticate by
  * using the client auth struct flavor field to index into svcauthsw.
@@ -93,6 +95,16 @@
 	rqst->rq_xprt->xp_verf.oa_length = 0;
 	cred_flavor = rqst->rq_cred.oa_flavor;
 	*no_dispatch = FALSE;
+
+	/* xp_auth is currently retained across calls for RPCSEC_GSS.  If the
+	 * client switched to a different auth flavor, destroy it. */
+	if (rqst->rq_xprt->xp_auth != NULL &&
+	    rqst->rq_xprt->xp_auth->svc_ah_ops == &svc_auth_gss_ops &&
+	    cred_flavor != RPCSEC_GSS) {
+	    SVCAUTH_DESTROY(rqst->rq_xprt->xp_auth);
+	    rqst->rq_xprt->xp_auth = NULL;
+	}
+
 	for (i = 0; i < svcauthnum; i++) {
 	     if (cred_flavor == svcauthsw[i].flavor &&
 		 svcauthsw[i].authenticator != NULL) {
Description: CVE-2026-11850 - Prevent read overrun in libkdb_ldap
 In berval2tl_data(), reject inputs of length less than 2 to prevent an
 integer underflow and subsequent read overrun. When bv_len is 0 or 1,
 the unsigned subtraction (bv_len - 2) wraps and is truncated to
 uint16_t, producing 0xFFFE/0xFFFF and causing a heap out-of-bounds
 read in the subsequent memcpy.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/krb5/krb5/commit/2a5fd83d4436583f2ddc0e193269a4d800ee45c4
Author: Sebastián Alba <sebasjosue84@gmail.com>
Last-Update: 2026-06-12
---
--- a/src/plugins/kdb/ldap/libkdb_ldap/ldap_principal2.c
+++ b/src/plugins/kdb/ldap/libkdb_ldap/ldap_principal2.c
@@ -80,6 +80,9 @@ getstringtime(krb5_timestamp);
 krb5_error_code
 berval2tl_data(struct berval *in, krb5_tl_data **out)
 {
+    if (in->bv_len < 2)
+        return EINVAL;
+
     *out = (krb5_tl_data *) malloc (sizeof (krb5_tl_data));
     if (*out == NULL)
         return ENOMEM;
Description: CVE-2026-112314 - Fix leak in RPC client on mismatched ID
 In clnttcp_call(), before decoding a reply, free the verifier in
 reply_msg if one was allocated when decoding a previous reply.  This
 prevents a memory leak in GSS-RPC client programs when RPC replies with
 mismatched XIDs are received or authentication retries are triggered.
 .
 Backported from the Debian trixie krb5 patch for the same upstream commit.
 The diff applies cleanly to krb5 1.20.1-2+deb12u5 (bookworm).
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/krb5/krb5/commit/aac40ec59fd4ffa126e19749e85ddb913892fe53
Author: Julien Rische <jrische@redhat.com>
Last-Update: 2026-11-13
---
--- a/src/lib/rpc/clnt_tcp.c
+++ b/src/lib/rpc/clnt_tcp.c
@@ -254,7 +254,7 @@ clnttcp_call(
 {
 	struct ct_data *ct = h->cl_private;
 	XDR *xdrs = &ct->ct_xdrs;
-	struct rpc_msg reply_msg;
+	struct rpc_msg reply_msg = { 0 };
 	uint32_t x_id;
 	uint32_t *msg_x_id = &ct->ct_u.ct_mcalli;	/* yuk */
 	bool_t shipnow;
@@ -299,6 +299,11 @@ call_again:
 	 */
 	xdrs->x_op = XDR_DECODE;
 	while (TRUE) {
+		/* Free verifier buffer if set from previous decode. */
+		if (reply_msg.rm_reply.rp_stat == MSG_ACCEPTED) {
+		    xdr_free((xdrproc_t)xdr_opaque_auth,
+			     &reply_msg.acpted_rply.ar_verf);
+		}
 		reply_msg.acpted_rply.ar_verf = gssrpc__null_auth;
 		reply_msg.acpted_rply.ar_results.where = NULL;
 		reply_msg.acpted_rply.ar_results.proc = xdr_void;
Description: CVE-2026-112323 - Disable GSSRPC AUTH_GSSAPI flavor by default
